    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d474-a1">

                <pb facs="0856" n="756" sameAs="frus:frus1880/pg756"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure in No. 29.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Mr. Ruelas.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1880-06-15"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 15,
                        1880</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: My government is informed that seventeen
                    Mexicans, who had been arrested by General Treviño for depredations committed
                    upon the property of American citizens, upon American soil, and who had been
                    sent by General Treviño to a prison in the interior of the country—city of
                    Mexico—have been released and returned to the scene of their former illegal
                    acts, at the expense of the Mexican Government.</p>
                <p>I am instructed to ascertain whether these reputed facts exist, and I therefore
                    address myself to your excellency.</p>
                <p>I renew to your excellency the assurances of my very distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. MORGAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
